# M12 nginx rate limiting — SUPERSEDES the stale numbers in nginx-m1.snippet.
#
# Applied via a NEW /etc/nginx/conf.d file so the shared /etc/nginx/nginx.conf is NEVER
# edited. slowapi already enforces per-route app-level limits; nginx here is only a
# coarse backstop ABOVE those, so it should never be the first limiter to trip.
#
# PRE-FLIGHT GATE (required): confirm the stock conf.d include exists —
#     nginx -T | grep 'include /etc/nginx/conf.d/\*.conf'
#   If it is ABSENT on this box, DEFER this step entirely (the only alternative is editing
#   the shared nginx.conf, not worth it on a many-project box) and record the deferral in
#   docs/OPS.md. If present, proceed.
#
# 1) NEW FILE /etc/nginx/conf.d/tilla-limit-req.conf — zone definitions ONLY (zones are
#    inert until referenced, so this file alone cannot affect any other vhost):
#
#      limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=tilla_api:10m rate=120r/m;
#      limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=tilla_create:10m rate=12r/m;
#
#    Note: the M1 snippet's 20r/m would 429 legitimate buyers — the checkout page polls
#    order status every few seconds and the app itself allows 40/min on status alone.
#    120r/m (2r/s) keeps nginx a backstop above slowapi, never the first to trip.
#
# 2) Edit ONLY /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/tilla.gudman.xyz.conf (back it up first). Add the
#    limit_req line inside each location, keeping the existing proxy_pass/headers:
#
#      location /api/ {
#          limit_req zone=tilla_api burst=30 nodelay;
#          client_max_body_size 128k;
#          proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8040;
#          # ... existing proxy_set_header lines ...
#      }
#
#      # /create-store, /upgrade-store, /add-product (the paid ASP routes):
#      location /create-store {
#          limit_req zone=tilla_create burst=5 nodelay;
#          client_max_body_size 128k;
#          proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8040;
#          # ... existing proxy_set_header lines ...
#      }
#      # (repeat the same block for location /upgrade-store and location /add-product)
#
# 3) Apply:  nginx -t  then  systemctl reload nginx   (reload, NEVER restart).
#
# Smoke: store page 200; checkout status poll at 1 req/3s stays 200; a ~40-request rapid
#   curl loop on /api/ trips 429 past the burst; unpaid POST /create-store still 402.
# Rollback: restore the vhost backup, rm /etc/nginx/conf.d/tilla-limit-req.conf,
#   nginx -t, systemctl reload nginx.
#
# Do NOT touch any other location block or vhost on this box (shared VPS — ground rules).
